const strip=h=>String(h||'').replace(/<sup>/g,'^').replace(/<sub>/g,'_').replace(/<[^>]+>/g,' ').replace(/&lt;/g,'<').replace(/&gt;/g,'>').replace(/&amp;/g,'&').replace(/\s+/g,' ').trim();
function flagQ(){const q=RD&&RD.queue[RD.i];if(!q)return;const ans=(q.options.find(o=>o.key===q.answer)||{}).html;S.flags=(S.flags||[]).concat({nk:q.nk,topic:REG[q.nk].name,q:strip(q.prompt).slice(0,500),a:strip(ans).slice(0,200),at:dayStr()}).slice(-50);save();const b=document.querySelector('[data-act=flag]');if(b){b.textContent='Flagged';b.disabled=true}toast('Flagged. It’s listed in Settings.','check')}
function flagsText(){return(S.flags||[]).map((f,i)=>`${i+1}. [${f.topic}] ${f.q}\n   App's answer: ${f.a}`).join('\n\n')}
function flags(){const fl=S.flags||[];modal(`<div class="box-h"><h2 class="t-title">Flagged questions</h2><button class="icon-btn close" data-act="close" aria-label="Close">${ic('x')}</button></div>
  ${fl.length?`<p class="help" style="margin:0 0 12px">Copy these and paste them to Claude to get them checked and fixed.</p><textarea class="codebox" id="xcode" readonly rows="8" aria-label="Flagged questions">${esc(flagsText())}</textarea>
  <div class="stack" style="margin-top:12px"><button class="btn btn-primary btn-block" data-act="flagcopy">Copy all</button><button class="btn btn-ghost btn-block" data-act="flagclear" style="color:var(--bad)">Clear the list</button><button class="btn btn-ghost btn-block" data-act="settings">Back to settings</button></div>`
  :`<p class="help" style="margin:0 0 16px">Nothing flagged yet. After answering, tap Flag on any question that looks wrong or unclear.</p><button class="btn btn-ghost btn-block" data-act="settings">Back to settings</button>`}`)}
let SQ='';
function searchHits(q){q=q.trim().toLowerCase();if(q.length<2)return[];const out=[];for(const c of COURSES)for(const w of c.worlds)for(const n of w.nodes){const x=LX[n.key]||{};const hay=[n.name,w.title,c.name,...(x.keys||[]).map(k=>k[0]+' '+k[1])].join(' ').toLowerCase();const inName=(n.name+' '+w.title).toLowerCase().includes(q);if(inName||hay.includes(q))out.push({n,w,c,score:inName?0:1})}return out.sort((a,b)=>a.score-b.score).slice(0,20)}
function renderSearch(){const box=$('#srch');if(!box)return;const hits=searchHits(SQ);box.innerHTML=SQ.trim().length<2?'':hits.length?`<div class="group">${hits.map(({n,w,c})=>`<button class="row" data-act="node" data-id="${n.key}" style="--course:var(--c-${c.id})">${markEl(n.key)}<span class="main-t"><span class="t">${n.name}</span><span class="s">${c.name}, ${esc(w.title)}</span></span><span class="end">${ic('chev',16)}</span></button>`).join('')}</div>`:`<p class="help" style="padding:8px 2px">No topics match “${esc(SQ.trim())}”. Try a term like gcd, limit or VSEPR.</p>`;document.querySelector('.chapters')&&(document.querySelector('.chapters').hidden=SQ.trim().length>=2)}
document.addEventListener('input',e=>{if(e.target.id==='tsearch'){SQ=e.target.value;renderSearch()}if(e.target.closest&&e.target.closest('.exform')){const x=$('#exerr');if(x)x.textContent=''}});
